hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22684","Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Muqri, narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Abu Isa al-Khurasani narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Qasim, who said: A neighboring woman of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, that she used to hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say at the rising of dawn: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave and from the trial of the grave. Abu Isa said: So I said to Abd Allah: What do you think if a man joins them? He said: Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said what he said."
